   "id": "temurah.14a.13",
   "daf": "14a",
   "sentenceId": 12,
   "he": "קׇרְבְּנוֹת יָחִיד חַיָּיבִין בְּאַחְרָיוּתָן [כּוּ׳]. מְנָא לַן?",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: If «offerings of an individual» were not brought at the appropriate time, one is «obligated to» bring «their compensation» and compensation for their accompanying meal offering and libations at a later date, whereas if communal offerings were not brought at the appropriate time, one is obligated to bring neither their compensation nor compensation for their accompanying meal offering and libations at a later date. The Gemara asks: «From where do we» derive this halakha, that if a communal offering was not sacrificed at the appropriate time it is not brought at a later stage?"
  }
